1
00:00:05,896 --> 00:00:07,016
[SPEAKER_01]: Are you liable to suffering?

2
00:00:09,377 --> 00:00:09,638
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

3
00:00:11,238 --> 00:00:16,620
[SPEAKER_00]: How?

4
00:00:17,181 --> 00:00:30,666
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, things can happen, on account of which, I wouldn't be pleased.

5
00:00:34,248 --> 00:00:34,988
[SPEAKER_00]: So, is that a problem?

6
00:00:40,648 --> 00:00:44,751
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, I mean, I'm just saying I still make a problem out of things, yeah.

7
00:00:45,852 --> 00:00:47,213
[SPEAKER_01]: No, I mean, suffering is the problem.

8
00:00:47,733 --> 00:00:48,734
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you're liable to it.

9
00:00:50,115 --> 00:00:51,156
[SPEAKER_00]: Suffering is the problem.

10
00:00:51,636 --> 00:00:53,618
[SPEAKER_00]: Is it the problem?

11
00:00:53,638 --> 00:00:59,742
[SPEAKER_00]: Your liability to it.

12
00:01:04,906 --> 00:01:05,126
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

13
00:01:06,787 --> 00:01:07,428
[SPEAKER_01]: How do you know that?

14
00:01:11,378 --> 00:01:15,301
[SPEAKER_01]: Because obviously nothing now is happening that's displeasing you in the present moment.

15
00:01:15,742 --> 00:01:15,982
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

16
00:01:16,602 --> 00:01:16,963
[SPEAKER_00]: It's funny.

17
00:01:16,983 --> 00:01:19,505
[SPEAKER_01]: So, how do you know that liability to suffering is a problem?

18
00:01:24,669 --> 00:01:26,731
[SPEAKER_00]: I guess the thought of the possibility of suffering.

19
00:01:28,152 --> 00:01:29,273
[SPEAKER_01]: But how do you know it's a problem?

20
00:01:29,654 --> 00:01:30,674
[SPEAKER_01]: Or otherwise it's a problem?

21
00:01:30,694 --> 00:01:31,255
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

22
00:01:37,480 --> 00:01:45,046
[SPEAKER_00]: So, this thought of the possibility of suffering... Just the possibility of suffering.

23
00:01:45,066 --> 00:01:46,267
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, the possibility of suffering.

24
00:01:47,568 --> 00:01:51,691
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's automatically assumed to be a problem.

25
00:01:53,252 --> 00:01:53,493
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

26
00:01:53,873 --> 00:01:54,914
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

27
00:01:54,934 --> 00:01:57,176
[SPEAKER_01]: And why is it assumed to be a problem?

28
00:02:00,738 --> 00:02:02,099
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a right assumption, by the way.

29
00:02:02,179 --> 00:02:02,840
[SPEAKER_01]: It is a problem.

30
00:02:04,601 --> 00:02:05,282
[SPEAKER_01]: But how do you know?

31
00:02:06,259 --> 00:02:06,879
[SPEAKER_01]: How do you know that?

32
00:02:06,939 --> 00:02:07,820
[SPEAKER_01]: How do you know it's a problem?

33
00:02:10,722 --> 00:02:11,462
[SPEAKER_01]: What is the measure?

34
00:02:12,683 --> 00:02:13,103
[SPEAKER_01]: Craving.

35
00:02:13,203 --> 00:02:13,524
[SPEAKER_01]: Fear.

36
00:02:15,245 --> 00:02:16,986
[SPEAKER_01]: What is the necessary base for craving?

37
00:02:18,006 --> 00:02:19,688
[SPEAKER_00]: Feeling.

38
00:02:19,728 --> 00:02:20,968
[SPEAKER_01]: So, what is... how is it felt?

39
00:02:21,329 --> 00:02:21,749
[SPEAKER_01]: Unpleasant.

40
00:02:22,369 --> 00:02:24,531
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's why it's a problem?

41
00:02:24,551 --> 00:02:24,771
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

42
00:02:24,931 --> 00:02:26,392
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you already suffer.

43
00:02:26,732 --> 00:02:26,952
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

44
00:02:27,112 --> 00:02:28,873
[SPEAKER_01]: On the fact that you don't suffer right now.

45
00:02:29,013 --> 00:02:29,314
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

46
00:02:29,594 --> 00:02:30,654
[SPEAKER_01]: But you could suffer.

47
00:02:30,674 --> 00:02:30,915
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

48
00:02:31,715 --> 00:02:33,696
[SPEAKER_01]: So, possibility of suffering is suffering.

49
00:02:34,337 --> 00:02:34,537
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

50
00:02:36,100 --> 00:02:46,351
[SPEAKER_01]: And the reason why I went in that direction is because... it can sound as if... oh, well, things can change and then I'll suffer.

51
00:02:46,371 --> 00:02:46,892
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

52
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:53,825
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means I'd have to wait for things to change, or try to prevent them from changing, in order to be dealing with the suffering.

53
00:02:53,885 --> 00:02:56,267
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, I mean, even some people often...

54
00:02:56,287 --> 00:02:59,370
[SPEAKER_00]: I heard people saying, oh, we all know what freeing from suffering is like.

55
00:02:59,390 --> 00:02:59,570
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

56
00:02:59,590 --> 00:03:02,313
[SPEAKER_01]: There are those occasions when everything is lovely, we don't suffer.

57
00:03:02,453 --> 00:03:03,133
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the point.

58
00:03:03,193 --> 00:03:06,216
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you not suffering now, doesn't mean you're free from suffering.

59
00:03:06,316 --> 00:03:06,576
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

60
00:03:07,577 --> 00:03:12,862
[SPEAKER_01]: And... or you suffering now, again, doesn't mean you're under suffering, so to speak.

61
00:03:13,593 --> 00:03:19,875
[SPEAKER_01]: You're under suffering, when basically on the level of possibility of suffering, you don't know the escape from that.

62
00:03:19,895 --> 00:03:20,515
[SPEAKER_01]: That's it, yeah.

63
00:03:20,655 --> 00:03:21,335
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what it is.

64
00:03:21,615 --> 00:03:22,655
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not knowing the escape.

65
00:03:23,236 --> 00:03:31,618
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the actually enduring suffering, if there is presently suffering, presently there is a feeling that's unpleasant, or absence of presently enduring suffering, doesn't matter.

66
00:03:32,238 --> 00:03:36,179
[SPEAKER_01]: Suffering is there, because you're still liable to the possibility of suffering.

67
00:03:36,459 --> 00:03:36,719
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

68
00:03:37,819 --> 00:03:38,680
[SPEAKER_01]: And that is present.

69
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:40,180
[SPEAKER_00]: Can I say it's not like...

70
00:03:44,076 --> 00:03:47,118
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not being confident of being able to...

71
00:03:57,484 --> 00:03:59,966
[SPEAKER_00]: It's like... maybe I'm wrong here.

72
00:04:00,186 --> 00:04:03,968
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, I don't feel like I've got no idea about the escape from suffering.

73
00:04:04,809 --> 00:04:11,173
[SPEAKER_00]: But it's not confidence of, like,

74
00:04:13,013 --> 00:04:18,775
[SPEAKER_00]: No matter what happened, the escape is known.

75
00:04:20,356 --> 00:04:21,617
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, that's the thing, yeah.

76
00:04:22,357 --> 00:04:23,357
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you don't know the escape.

77
00:04:23,397 --> 00:04:23,678
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

78
00:04:24,578 --> 00:04:26,479
[SPEAKER_00]: Because the escape is...

79
00:04:27,319 --> 00:04:27,719
[SPEAKER_00]: Complete.

80
00:04:28,259 --> 00:04:32,561
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, it's complete, but it's also... it's not dependent on the type of suffering.

81
00:04:33,482 --> 00:04:38,564
[SPEAKER_01]: Escape of suffering means escape of nature of suffering, which means it doesn't matter what the content of that nature is.

82
00:04:38,584 --> 00:04:38,804
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

83
00:04:40,199 --> 00:04:43,502
[SPEAKER_01]: In other words, it's not like sometimes you escape like this, sometimes you escape like that.

84
00:04:44,463 --> 00:04:52,289
[SPEAKER_01]: The escape from suffering is the escape from that liability to the nature of suffering, which means then it doesn't matter what causes it.

85
00:04:52,930 --> 00:04:56,753
[SPEAKER_01]: You won't need to deal with it, because you don't suffer on account of it, at that fundamental level.

86
00:04:57,694 --> 00:05:04,279
[SPEAKER_01]: So, why do you think then there is not enough confidence in you to know the way out of suffering?

87
00:05:06,401 --> 00:05:07,062
[SPEAKER_01]: What is the reason?

88
00:05:17,574 --> 00:05:19,256
[SPEAKER_01]: So, think about it on the level of feeling.

89
00:05:20,777 --> 00:05:21,618
[SPEAKER_01]: Unpleasant feeling.

90
00:05:21,738 --> 00:05:22,038
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

91
00:05:22,839 --> 00:05:23,179
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay.

92
00:05:24,581 --> 00:05:25,201
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's...

93
00:05:25,221 --> 00:05:26,422
[SPEAKER_00]: I guess that's one way of putting it.

94
00:05:26,462 --> 00:05:26,863
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

95
00:05:27,003 --> 00:05:31,787
[SPEAKER_00]: It's like not liking unpleasant feeling.

96
00:05:35,111 --> 00:05:42,818
[SPEAKER_00]: Not having, again, confidence in being able to withstand any kind of feeling.

97
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:44,621
[SPEAKER_00]: No matter how unpleasant.

98
00:05:45,922 --> 00:05:55,128
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the whole variety of feelings, where can they be felt?

99
00:05:55,168 --> 00:05:55,969
[SPEAKER_00]: Where can they be felt?

100
00:05:55,989 --> 00:05:56,129
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

101
00:05:56,970 --> 00:05:58,231
[SPEAKER_00]: Where can feelings be felt?

102
00:05:58,311 --> 00:06:03,334
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, like, colorfully speaking, where can you feel those, all the feelings that could possibly befall you?

103
00:06:03,495 --> 00:06:04,575
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, the body?

104
00:06:05,236 --> 00:06:05,756
[SPEAKER_00]: The body.

105
00:06:06,457 --> 00:06:07,678
[SPEAKER_01]: And where else?

106
00:06:08,678 --> 00:06:09,019
[SPEAKER_01]: Or when?

107
00:06:10,079 --> 00:06:10,900
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, right here.

108
00:06:12,519 --> 00:06:12,859
[SPEAKER_01]: Right now.

109
00:06:13,120 --> 00:06:14,020
[SPEAKER_01]: Right now.

110
00:06:15,462 --> 00:06:20,066
[SPEAKER_01]: So, can you feel the feeling in the past?

111
00:06:20,166 --> 00:06:20,447
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

112
00:06:21,448 --> 00:06:22,068
[SPEAKER_00]: Inconceivable.

113
00:06:22,088 --> 00:06:23,089
[SPEAKER_00]: Absolutely inconceivable.

114
00:06:23,890 --> 00:06:25,572
[SPEAKER_01]: And can you feel the feeling in the future?

115
00:06:26,349 --> 00:06:29,511
[SPEAKER_00]: No, but it's easy to assume that you can.

116
00:06:30,172 --> 00:06:30,992
[SPEAKER_00]: But yes, you can't.

117
00:06:31,012 --> 00:06:34,254
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, it's easy if carelessness is your mode of being.

118
00:06:34,294 --> 00:06:35,795
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

119
00:06:35,855 --> 00:06:38,697
[SPEAKER_01]: That's sure, that needs to be dealt with beforehand.

120
00:06:39,438 --> 00:06:46,182
[SPEAKER_01]: So, literally, it doesn't matter what past feeling you might remember, what future feeling you might fear or hope for.

121
00:06:46,242 --> 00:06:46,502
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

122
00:06:47,063 --> 00:06:47,963
[SPEAKER_01]: It's felt right now.

123
00:06:47,983 --> 00:06:48,484
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah.

124
00:06:49,985 --> 00:06:55,048
[SPEAKER_01]: So, as a container, in itself, present enduring feeling can only be felt now.

125
00:06:56,586 --> 00:06:59,467
[SPEAKER_01]: And it's inconceivable to make it otherwise.

126
00:06:59,747 --> 00:07:09,249
[SPEAKER_01]: You actually have to ignore it, have to actively engage with acts and decisions and choices that will kind of enable you to ignore the fact that it is felt now.

127
00:07:09,349 --> 00:07:10,929
[SPEAKER_01]: It cannot not be felt now.

128
00:07:11,169 --> 00:07:11,789
[SPEAKER_01]: It's impossible.

129
00:07:13,730 --> 00:07:20,111
[SPEAKER_01]: You see, you've talked a lot recently about containers, this nature of containment.

130
00:07:21,825 --> 00:07:27,189
[SPEAKER_01]: That's one of the the characteristics of containment, that it's... it's now.

131
00:07:28,170 --> 00:07:28,810
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, of course.

132
00:07:28,871 --> 00:07:29,591
[SPEAKER_00]: It can't not be.

133
00:07:29,731 --> 00:07:32,013
[SPEAKER_01]: The foundations of mindfulness, yeah, it's not optional.

134
00:07:32,113 --> 00:07:32,333
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

135
00:07:39,479 --> 00:07:47,205
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why the one who understands that, as we said, he stops thinking like, oh, now I understood the nature of feelings and the nature of anatta.

136
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:48,961
[SPEAKER_01]: In the past, I was.

137
00:07:49,061 --> 00:07:49,781
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, I'm not.

138
00:07:50,021 --> 00:07:51,022
[SPEAKER_01]: In the future, I will not.

139
00:07:51,042 --> 00:07:55,004
[SPEAKER_01]: None of that becomes... well, all of that ceases to be intelligible, to think like that.

140
00:07:55,805 --> 00:07:57,666
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, I was before, because it's not a linear thing.

141
00:07:58,886 --> 00:08:01,848
[SPEAKER_01]: Whatever it's felt right here, right now, that's what has been understood.

142
00:08:02,128 --> 00:08:02,328
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

143
00:08:02,348 --> 00:08:05,911
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what whatever has the nature arising, it has been understood.

144
00:08:06,971 --> 00:08:08,192
[SPEAKER_01]: I guess most people think of

145
00:08:10,994 --> 00:08:14,936
[SPEAKER_00]: The past, the future and stuff, as like, as, as like a... Yeah.

146
00:08:14,996 --> 00:08:15,497
[SPEAKER_00]: Objective.

147
00:08:15,517 --> 00:08:16,097
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, exactly.

148
00:08:16,117 --> 00:08:19,839
[SPEAKER_01]: It's an external view upon yourself that you have.

149
00:08:20,259 --> 00:08:27,603
[SPEAKER_01]: Like you are in this objective, factual world that you can observe independent of your point of view of observation.

150
00:08:27,764 --> 00:08:27,944
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

151
00:08:28,084 --> 00:08:29,064
[SPEAKER_01]: Which is inconceivable.

152
00:08:32,006 --> 00:08:37,209
[SPEAKER_01]: But back onto the practical side of things, more relevant in this case now, while we're speaking.

153
00:08:38,083 --> 00:08:56,067
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you presently recognize that you are liable to suffering, the extent of your liability to suffering cannot be anywhere else except within that presently enduring feeling of suffering, on account of possibility to suffer.

154
00:08:58,367 --> 00:09:04,428
[SPEAKER_01]: So, anything that needs to be understood cannot be anywhere else except in the present.

155
00:09:06,669 --> 00:09:07,069
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

156
00:09:07,718 --> 00:09:13,800
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it might take you five days to understand it, but it will be five days of understanding what's presently enduring.

157
00:09:14,921 --> 00:09:18,022
[SPEAKER_01]: Not like in five days I will arrive at something that's not here now.

158
00:09:18,862 --> 00:09:20,343
[SPEAKER_01]: It is here now, it's just cluttered.

159
00:09:21,663 --> 00:09:26,485
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it might take you a number of days to unclutter it, while it is still here now.

160
00:09:45,012 --> 00:09:55,180
[SPEAKER_01]: And the extent of that liability to suffering, whatever it is, directly corresponds to the extent that you haven't understood, presently during pain.

161
00:09:55,260 --> 00:09:55,481
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

162
00:09:58,323 --> 00:10:02,827
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you start thinking like this, you realize there's... What is it stopping you then?

163
00:10:03,087 --> 00:10:03,327
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

164
00:10:03,447 --> 00:10:04,168
[SPEAKER_00]: From understanding it?

165
00:10:08,972 --> 00:10:11,273
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just a simple attitude to this feeling.

166
00:10:11,534 --> 00:10:14,236
[SPEAKER_00]: That's... That's that.

167
00:10:15,215 --> 00:10:15,415
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

168
00:10:15,977 --> 00:10:22,330
[SPEAKER_01]: Attitude that then needs to be peeled off, bit by bit, layer by layer.

169
00:10:55,175 --> 00:11:08,101
[SPEAKER_00]: So, like, it's allowing the currently enduring feeling to just endure, not trying to get involved in it.

170
00:11:08,701 --> 00:11:21,087
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, but you can't completely ignore it either, in the sense of you can get overly involved, sure, but you can also get underly involved, so to speak.

171
00:11:21,627 --> 00:11:22,108
[SPEAKER_01]: In other words,

172
00:11:23,315 --> 00:11:25,717
[SPEAKER_01]: You do have a task of... you must understand it.

173
00:11:25,817 --> 00:11:26,698
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

174
00:11:26,718 --> 00:11:30,501
[SPEAKER_01]: So, how can you understand it without over... without getting overly involved with it?

175
00:11:30,541 --> 00:11:32,743
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

176
00:11:32,763 --> 00:11:35,045
[SPEAKER_01]: So, either way, yeah, it needs to endure there.

177
00:11:35,706 --> 00:11:38,348
[SPEAKER_00]: You must stop denying it, you must stop acting out of it.

178
00:11:40,270 --> 00:11:43,873
[SPEAKER_00]: Just like the automated act towards craving as a habit.

179
00:11:49,698 --> 00:11:57,622
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you also can re-evaluate, on account of presently enduring feeling, whatever that feeling is, you can re-evaluate the extent of your liability to suffering.

180
00:11:58,262 --> 00:12:00,463
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, am I still liable to suffering?

181
00:12:01,803 --> 00:12:02,524
[SPEAKER_00]: To what degree?

182
00:12:03,844 --> 00:12:11,988
[SPEAKER_00]: Would you say, so then understanding the sort of the current feeling involves

183
00:12:19,138 --> 00:12:26,201
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, eh... recognizing that I was subjected to it.

184
00:12:29,242 --> 00:12:30,383
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, sure, that's part of it.

185
00:12:30,963 --> 00:12:33,524
[SPEAKER_01]: It's... you don't always have to go the same way about it.

186
00:12:34,364 --> 00:12:36,645
[SPEAKER_01]: What you need to do is recognize that there is something felt.

187
00:12:37,146 --> 00:12:37,326
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

188
00:12:39,347 --> 00:12:43,328
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, see in what fundamental category that will be sitting in.

189
00:12:44,589 --> 00:12:47,490
[SPEAKER_01]: Pleasant, unpleasant, or neither pleasant nor unpleasant.

190
00:12:48,396 --> 00:12:54,199
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, that's already, you know, being able to see that already means, oh, this is something you are subjected to.

191
00:12:54,519 --> 00:13:00,321
[SPEAKER_01]: See, you can say, I have this pleasant feeling, this pleasant feeling is mine, and that's why I'm acting, protecting it, trying to get more of it.

192
00:13:00,881 --> 00:13:04,123
[SPEAKER_01]: But you have absolutely no say in its pleasantness.

193
00:13:05,323 --> 00:13:07,664
[SPEAKER_01]: You cannot create pleasantness of the pleasant feeling.

194
00:13:08,004 --> 00:13:08,885
[SPEAKER_01]: You can only accept it.

195
00:13:09,145 --> 00:13:09,365
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

196
00:13:10,505 --> 00:13:13,387
[SPEAKER_01]: So, what makes pleasantness of the pleasant feeling?

197
00:13:13,447 --> 00:13:14,807
[SPEAKER_01]: It's inconceivable to you.

198
00:13:14,867 --> 00:13:16,088
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just felt pleasantly.

199
00:13:16,148 --> 00:13:16,428
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

200
00:13:17,162 --> 00:13:25,729
[SPEAKER_01]: You can try and rationalize afterwards, as an afterthought and so on, but all of that is in response to being subjected to the pleasantness of a feeling.

201
00:13:25,749 --> 00:13:26,029
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

202
00:13:26,609 --> 00:13:29,111
[SPEAKER_01]: And same to the unpleasantness of a feeling.

203
00:13:35,396 --> 00:13:42,601
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why you realize you cannot possibly, eh... uproot that.

204
00:13:42,621 --> 00:13:45,764
[SPEAKER_01]: You cannot get under it and, like, take the possession over it.

205
00:13:50,132 --> 00:14:06,763
[SPEAKER_01]: So, clarifying that type of image, context, understanding, discernment, and then also preventing the increasing of the clutter, of cover-up, through the acts rooted in greed, aversion, delusion.

206
00:14:07,523 --> 00:14:10,005
[SPEAKER_01]: So, sense restraint and watchfulness.

207
00:14:11,162 --> 00:14:13,223
[SPEAKER_00]: Not watchfulness for, like, who knows what purpose.

208
00:14:13,243 --> 00:14:13,523
[SPEAKER_00]: I don't know.

209
00:14:13,563 --> 00:14:15,365
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm just watchful, watchful, watchful.

210
00:14:15,825 --> 00:14:16,605
[SPEAKER_01]: No, you know exactly.

211
00:14:16,805 --> 00:14:19,767
[SPEAKER_01]: The present feeling, presently arisen feeling endures.

212
00:14:20,768 --> 00:14:28,392
[SPEAKER_01]: And if I'm not mindful of its endurance on its own, independent of me, I will be acting out of the craving towards it.

213
00:14:28,612 --> 00:14:29,333
[SPEAKER_01]: It's automatic.

214
00:14:29,513 --> 00:14:29,693
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

215
00:14:30,173 --> 00:14:33,295
[SPEAKER_01]: All you need to do is accept ignorance, ignoring it.

216
00:14:34,296 --> 00:14:36,157
[SPEAKER_01]: Accept turning your blind eye to it.

217
00:14:36,517 --> 00:14:38,078
[SPEAKER_01]: Accept desire for distraction.

218
00:14:38,468 --> 00:14:40,769
[SPEAKER_01]: And everything else will follow effortlessly.

219
00:14:41,869 --> 00:14:42,629
[SPEAKER_01]: Like floodgates.

220
00:14:42,749 --> 00:14:45,650
[SPEAKER_01]: All you need to do is open it, then all the pressure will just flow out.

221
00:14:51,612 --> 00:14:56,494
[SPEAKER_01]: But within, like, within the mindfulness of present enduring feeling, yeah, you can do whatever you want.

222
00:14:57,294 --> 00:14:58,774
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you won't be doing anything unwholesome.

223
00:14:59,314 --> 00:15:05,756
[SPEAKER_01]: Because in order to do unwholesome things, you need to be unmindful of the present, the nature of the present enduring feeling.

224
00:15:05,896 --> 00:15:07,777
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't do unwholesome things mindfully.

225
00:15:11,297 --> 00:15:20,439
[SPEAKER_00]: And then the understanding can only develop if whatever you're doing is within... Yeah, sure, sure.

226
00:15:20,579 --> 00:15:21,840
[SPEAKER_01]: And not contradicting it.

227
00:15:22,020 --> 00:15:22,840
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly, exactly.

228
00:15:22,860 --> 00:15:28,161
[SPEAKER_01]: Then you're becoming familiar with the nature of how feeling actually is.

229
00:15:30,041 --> 00:15:31,902
[SPEAKER_01]: Not how you keep conceiving it to be.

230
00:15:36,580 --> 00:15:39,823
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the thing that can't be conceived, really, can it?

231
00:15:39,843 --> 00:15:42,505
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it's... Well, that's true for an arahant.

232
00:15:42,765 --> 00:15:43,225
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

233
00:15:44,006 --> 00:15:49,210
[SPEAKER_01]: See, you... somebody who is still conceiving the feeling, saying the feeling cannot truly be conceived, it's true only in theory.

234
00:15:49,310 --> 00:15:49,550
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

235
00:15:49,990 --> 00:15:54,434
[SPEAKER_01]: But that contradicts his actual state of mind that does conceive it.

236
00:15:54,634 --> 00:15:54,774
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

237
00:15:55,175 --> 00:15:59,438
[SPEAKER_01]: So that's why we need to keep that in mind, because that's how people fall into the view that they think they understood.

238
00:15:59,458 --> 00:15:59,658
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

239
00:16:00,078 --> 00:16:04,822
[SPEAKER_01]: But the right view is, or what arahantship is, while they know they're still putujanas, that is inconceivable.

240
00:16:07,056 --> 00:16:13,558
[SPEAKER_01]: So, yeah, you might have an idea about it, and that idea is true, but it's far from being... having been applied to you.

241
00:16:15,318 --> 00:16:19,479
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, that's like in the suttas.

242
00:16:19,499 --> 00:16:25,101
[SPEAKER_01]: You probably have that difference between the knowledge and the direct knowledge, what sometimes they translate with.

243
00:16:25,481 --> 00:16:25,801
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

244
00:16:26,881 --> 00:16:27,641
[SPEAKER_00]: Abhijānāti.

245
00:16:54,711 --> 00:17:02,415
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it starts by being... just recollecting what is the... what feeling is enduring right here, right now, while we're talking.

246
00:17:04,495 --> 00:17:10,878
[SPEAKER_01]: And once you recollect, it's more than enough, as a container, as a base for mindfulness.

247
00:17:12,179 --> 00:17:14,100
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, when you think, what do I do next now?

248
00:17:15,144 --> 00:17:20,989
[SPEAKER_01]: Instead of following the thought of what do I do next, you see the need to do next within the container.

249
00:17:21,069 --> 00:17:21,489
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

250
00:17:21,609 --> 00:17:22,090
[SPEAKER_01]: Everything.

251
00:17:22,450 --> 00:17:23,411
[SPEAKER_01]: Everything is in that container.

252
00:17:23,431 --> 00:17:23,991
[SPEAKER_01]: Feeling is first.

253
00:17:24,271 --> 00:17:29,455
[SPEAKER_00]: And now, within this feeling, I have the state of mind that's doubtful and wondering what to do next.

254
00:17:29,595 --> 00:17:35,720
[SPEAKER_01]: And you don't do anything because all you need to do is stay rooted in the container that you recollected of presently enduring feeling.

255
00:17:36,381 --> 00:17:39,283
[SPEAKER_01]: That's how eventually you learn how to stop acting out feelings.

256
00:17:42,099 --> 00:17:45,540
[SPEAKER_01]: Which requires loss of that perspective of present enduring feeling.

257
00:17:45,560 --> 00:17:48,480
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there is unpleasant feeling and here I am.

258
00:17:49,541 --> 00:17:56,282
[SPEAKER_01]: Busying myself, acting, choosing to get rid of it, to understand it, to rationalize it, to deal with it, one way or the other, to manage it.

259
00:17:59,843 --> 00:18:02,363
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you're properly mindful, management becomes impossible.

260
00:18:02,984 --> 00:18:09,625
[SPEAKER_01]: Because any inclination towards management is included within present enduring feeling and that's effortless.

261
00:18:11,377 --> 00:18:12,358
[SPEAKER_01]: You're not managing anything.

262
00:18:13,599 --> 00:18:20,183
[SPEAKER_01]: You're actually subduing your dependence on craving the need to manage these things.

263
00:18:23,545 --> 00:18:25,867
[SPEAKER_01]: Subduing it by including it.

264
00:18:27,528 --> 00:18:30,630
[SPEAKER_01]: But you can't include it as a matter of your choice.

265
00:18:31,251 --> 00:18:33,652
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't decide, this is also included.

266
00:18:34,293 --> 00:18:35,554
[SPEAKER_01]: That's not including, I'm talking about.

267
00:18:38,496 --> 00:18:40,077
[SPEAKER_01]: You need to discern, recollect,

268
00:18:41,285 --> 00:18:42,449
[SPEAKER_01]: Presently enduring feeling.

269
00:18:42,830 --> 00:18:46,841
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, whatever is simultaneously there, that's why it's included.

270
00:18:46,881 --> 00:18:48,325
[SPEAKER_01]: Not because you made it so.

271
00:18:49,070 --> 00:18:54,595
[SPEAKER_01]: Because that's inevitably going to happen until the mind develops certain subtlety in regard to this.

272
00:18:54,655 --> 00:18:59,539
[SPEAKER_01]: You'll be... get the hint of it and then you go around including things.

273
00:18:59,719 --> 00:19:00,780
[SPEAKER_01]: You including them.

274
00:19:00,800 --> 00:19:01,621
[SPEAKER_00]: That's not including.

275
00:19:01,641 --> 00:19:06,866
[SPEAKER_00]: Which is why what you're talking about is also about understanding feeling.

276
00:19:06,906 --> 00:19:07,526
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

277
00:19:07,566 --> 00:19:08,047
[SPEAKER_01]: But there's a thing.

278
00:19:08,107 --> 00:19:10,349
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't need to stop including your things.

279
00:19:10,769 --> 00:19:11,670
[SPEAKER_01]: You just need to include

280
00:19:11,830 --> 00:19:14,351
[SPEAKER_01]: That attitude of including things.

281
00:19:14,411 --> 00:19:22,193
[SPEAKER_01]: And you would include that attitude not as a matter of choice, but as a matter of discernment, recollecting the right context, the right order.

282
00:19:22,653 --> 00:19:29,315
[SPEAKER_01]: Whatever I'm trying to include, whatever I'm trying to manage, whatever I'm trying to deal with, things that bother me, things that pull me, it doesn't matter.

283
00:19:30,195 --> 00:19:31,856
[SPEAKER_01]: It's within the present enduring feeling.

284
00:19:33,356 --> 00:19:38,017
[SPEAKER_01]: And whatever I were to do, whatever I used to do, it's within the present enduring feeling.

285
00:19:38,317 --> 00:19:40,058
[SPEAKER_01]: That order cannot be otherwise.

286
00:19:40,697 --> 00:19:44,960
[SPEAKER_01]: When that right order becomes imperturbable, yeah, that's basically your samādhi.

287
00:19:45,160 --> 00:19:47,201
[SPEAKER_01]: And there is already a great deal of wisdom there.

288
00:19:47,221 --> 00:19:49,723
[SPEAKER_01]: You cannot have that without understanding what's going on.

289
00:19:50,304 --> 00:19:51,705
[SPEAKER_01]: You just cannot.

290
00:19:51,725 --> 00:19:54,847
[SPEAKER_01]: So, like, I had this experience and now I need to understand what happened to me.

291
00:19:55,027 --> 00:19:56,848
[SPEAKER_01]: It means you have no idea what happened to you.

292
00:19:56,868 --> 00:20:00,471
[SPEAKER_01]: Now you're just going to reinterpret it, usually in the terms that will be pleasing you.

293
00:20:00,491 --> 00:20:00,751
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

294
00:20:01,952 --> 00:20:03,973
[SPEAKER_01]: Or playing into the views that you hope you have.

295
00:20:09,033 --> 00:20:14,535
[SPEAKER_00]: No, this is about... yes, it's... that samādhi is entirely based on your understanding.

296
00:20:14,935 --> 00:20:27,120
[SPEAKER_01]: So, against the context of present enduring feeling, that you recognize it's there or isn't, you're within it, you're subjected to it, you then also get to see the state of your mind.

297
00:20:28,380 --> 00:20:33,902
[SPEAKER_01]: Mind affected with doubt, mind free from doubt, mind that craves lust, sensuality, mind that doesn't.

298
00:20:34,243 --> 00:20:37,484
[SPEAKER_01]: It's calm, you know, you got sensuality, mind a bit annoyed, mind not annoyed.

299
00:20:38,553 --> 00:20:41,475
[SPEAKER_01]: Against or within the container of present enduring feeling.

300
00:20:42,716 --> 00:20:43,656
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, what do I do next?

301
00:20:43,876 --> 00:20:46,558
[SPEAKER_01]: You see that within the container of present enduring feeling.

302
00:20:47,719 --> 00:20:48,499
[SPEAKER_01]: So, I don't do anything?

303
00:20:48,599 --> 00:20:53,002
[SPEAKER_01]: You see that within the present enduring container of the present enduring feeling.

304
00:20:56,924 --> 00:20:57,725
[SPEAKER_00]: How long do I do this for?

305
00:20:58,805 --> 00:21:00,606
[SPEAKER_01]: Dhamma question included within it.

306
00:21:01,507 --> 00:21:02,728
[SPEAKER_01]: Feeling comes first.

307
00:21:02,748 --> 00:21:02,968
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

308
00:21:12,780 --> 00:21:14,981
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you're wondering also, what can I do then?

309
00:21:15,041 --> 00:21:18,122
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, you cannot do anything anymore.

310
00:21:18,403 --> 00:21:19,303
[SPEAKER_01]: But things will be done.

311
00:21:25,226 --> 00:21:27,467
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, there's no room to do anything anymore.

312
00:21:27,487 --> 00:21:27,727
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

313
00:21:29,107 --> 00:21:30,008
[SPEAKER_01]: You doing it.

314
00:21:30,068 --> 00:21:30,308
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

315
00:21:30,428 --> 00:21:33,369
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just... you'll just find things being done.

316
00:21:35,690 --> 00:21:41,773
[SPEAKER_01]: And by that point, it will be impossible for those things to be anything other than wholesome.

317
00:21:42,918 --> 00:21:43,439
[SPEAKER_01]: Or neutral.

318
00:21:45,500 --> 00:21:48,843
[SPEAKER_01]: They cannot be unwholesome, because that requires you choosing that.

319
00:21:49,303 --> 00:21:54,867
[SPEAKER_00]: Because unwholesome, sort of by definition, is perverting the order.

320
00:21:54,887 --> 00:21:55,968
[SPEAKER_01]: Perverting the order, exactly.

321
00:21:56,228 --> 00:22:00,331
[SPEAKER_01]: And now the order is imperturbable, thus whatever's done cannot be unwholesome.

322
00:22:01,092 --> 00:22:11,380
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why certain things sotāpanna cannot do, certain things arahant cannot do, like impossible to be done, because it requires a necessity of that wrong order.

323
00:22:12,588 --> 00:22:13,748
[SPEAKER_00]: Not seeing first is first.

324
00:22:16,430 --> 00:22:25,293
[SPEAKER_01]: Not seeing presently, enduring, feeling, whatever that feeling is, pleasant, unpleasant, neither pleasant nor unpleasant, is a necessary container for any act rooted in... in your craving.

325
00:22:25,993 --> 00:22:26,534
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't matter.

326
00:22:44,412 --> 00:22:50,013
[SPEAKER_01]: And you realize you'll be then quite content with whatever container there is.

327
00:22:50,153 --> 00:22:51,014
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't matter anymore.

328
00:22:51,394 --> 00:22:56,875
[SPEAKER_01]: Even unpleasant feelings, so to speak, will not be a source of unhappiness.

329
00:22:59,856 --> 00:23:04,017
[SPEAKER_01]: Because happy, unhappy, or content, discontent, is a state of your mind.

330
00:23:04,237 --> 00:23:05,537
[SPEAKER_00]: It's a content within the container.

331
00:23:05,677 --> 00:23:06,057
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

332
00:23:06,258 --> 00:23:11,839
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's basically a state of your mind that either it resists against the container, tries to, like,

333
00:23:12,849 --> 00:23:17,831
[SPEAKER_01]: Take possession of it, in order to free the whatever is bothering the mind.

334
00:23:18,312 --> 00:23:19,372
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's trying to deal with it.

335
00:23:19,412 --> 00:23:24,855
[SPEAKER_01]: There is always a pressure, a burden, a requirement of the duty, dealing with it, defending myself against these feelings.

336
00:23:25,575 --> 00:23:32,379
[SPEAKER_01]: All of that becomes inconceivable, because whatever the mind presents, it's seen within the right order of present enduring feeling.

337
00:23:32,759 --> 00:23:34,420
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's quite indifferent already.

338
00:23:34,700 --> 00:23:34,940
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

339
00:23:34,960 --> 00:23:38,562
[SPEAKER_00]: So, all of that resisting is actually about trying to

340
00:23:40,673 --> 00:23:42,194
[SPEAKER_00]: It involves trying to change the order.

341
00:23:42,354 --> 00:23:43,135
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, yeah.

342
00:23:43,455 --> 00:23:45,296
[SPEAKER_00]: Because you... Well, all that resisting...

343
00:23:45,436 --> 00:23:47,017
[SPEAKER_00]: I can control that container.

344
00:23:47,177 --> 00:23:47,377
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

345
00:23:47,818 --> 00:23:51,080
[SPEAKER_01]: All that resisting is rooted in assuming that you can change the order.

346
00:23:51,100 --> 00:23:51,260
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

347
00:23:52,441 --> 00:23:55,083
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's like... that's why... that's basically the definition of conceit.

348
00:23:55,403 --> 00:23:55,643
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

349
00:23:56,884 --> 00:24:07,451
[SPEAKER_01]: It's that subtle perversion whereby just your point of view assumes, to that extent, itself to be coming first.

350
00:24:12,111 --> 00:24:15,232
[SPEAKER_01]: So, then, you'll be happy amidst pain.

351
00:24:16,752 --> 00:24:18,373
[SPEAKER_01]: Not like enjoying it, sensually.

352
00:24:19,173 --> 00:24:24,014
[SPEAKER_01]: But you will not be discontent, even if there is unpleasant feeling enduring for days.

353
00:24:26,054 --> 00:24:29,235
[SPEAKER_01]: Because discontent is not in what feeling you're subjected to.

354
00:24:29,615 --> 00:24:29,815
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

355
00:24:29,895 --> 00:24:40,178
[SPEAKER_01]: Discontent is in that pressure of it, which goes hand in hand with you attempting to deal with it, manage it, remove it, crave against it, crave for it, whatever.

356
00:24:41,360 --> 00:24:45,103
[SPEAKER_00]: Exercise, basically, effort towards it.

357
00:24:45,583 --> 00:24:56,271
[SPEAKER_01]: Rather than... Rather than seeing that any effort you send, you might send, you want to send, you don't want to send, anything you send, yes, no, too, both, neither, is within that, and that cannot change.

358
00:24:56,872 --> 00:25:04,117
[SPEAKER_01]: So, even if you're trying to go towards it, to grab it, to deal with it, to remove it, to destroy it, to repossess it, it's always a step ahead.

359
00:25:04,137 --> 00:25:04,377
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

360
00:25:05,158 --> 00:25:08,060
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it's determined by how far you step, that's how far it goes.

361
00:25:09,371 --> 00:25:11,293
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you cannot possibly step outside of it.

362
00:25:16,257 --> 00:25:23,242
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you want to be happy, as in free from suffering, see what feeling is there, and doesn't matter if it's not happiness.

363
00:25:23,542 --> 00:25:23,823
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

364
00:25:24,663 --> 00:25:28,226
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, see that whatever attitude you have towards it... Yeah.

365
00:25:28,246 --> 00:25:29,147
[SPEAKER_01]: ...is within that.

366
00:25:29,187 --> 00:25:29,447
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

367
00:25:29,487 --> 00:25:30,288
[SPEAKER_01]: Not other way around.

368
00:25:30,708 --> 00:25:36,413
[SPEAKER_01]: And stick to that, and you will be unable to suffer, even if you were to want to suffer.

369
00:25:36,985 --> 00:25:37,165
[SPEAKER_01]: Hmm.

370
00:25:37,445 --> 00:25:38,505
[SPEAKER_01]: It becomes inconceivable.

371
00:25:38,526 --> 00:25:39,766
[SPEAKER_01]: Suffering becomes inconceivable.

372
00:25:40,006 --> 00:25:45,588
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

373
00:25:45,608 --> 00:25:48,188
[SPEAKER_00]: Very clear instructions.

374
00:25:48,329 --> 00:25:51,530
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

375
00:25:51,570 --> 00:25:52,390
[SPEAKER_01]: This needs to be done.

376
00:25:52,670 --> 00:25:52,910
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

377
00:25:55,651 --> 00:25:56,251
[SPEAKER_01]: Or maintained.

